      "side": 1,
      "message": "Prevent the single-backtick regex branch from matching across unclosed double-backtick delimiters.\n\nIn `tokenizeWords` (and `codeSpanRegex` in `renderInlineCodeSpans` below), if a paragraph contains an unclosed ` `` ` followed later by another ` ` ` (e.g. `foo ``bar`), the first branch ` ``(?:[^`\\n]|`[^`\\n])+`` ` fails to match at the first backtick, and at the second backtick the second branch `` `[^`\\n]+` `` matches `` `bar` ``, converting mismatched delimiter lengths into a `\u003ccode\u003e` span. Guarding single-backtick matches with `(?\u003c!`)`[^`\\n]+`(?!`)` (until replaced by `Lexer.lexInline` in change 643703) keeps mismatched backtick sequences as literal text.\n\n_from potto_",
